1
00:03:12,857 --> 00:03:18,857
Christmas Wonderland is a tv movie, romance film directed by Sean Olson.

2
00:06:25,714 --> 00:06:31,714
Heidi, who initially left her small town of Pleasant Valley with the dream of one day becoming a
successful painter, has put her own art on hold to excel as an art gallery curator.

3
00:09:38,571 --> 00:09:44,571
Now, a week before the gallery’s big Christmas party, she
must return home to watch her niece and nephew.

4
00:12:51,428 --> 00:12:57,428
She comes face to face with her high school love, Chris, now a teacher, and offers
to help him find a new last-minute location for the Christmas dance.

5
00:16:04,285 --> 00:16:10,285
Heidi Nelson, played by Emily Osment.

6
00:19:17,142 --> 00:19:23,142
Chris Shepherd, played by Ryan Rottman.

7
00:22:30,000 --> 00:22:36,000
Julia, played by Kelly Hu.

8
00:25:42,857 --> 00:25:48,857
Tom Westwood, played by Jacob Buster.

9
00:28:55,714 --> 00:29:01,714
Katie Westwood, played by Trinity Roberts.

10
00:32:08,571 --> 00:32:14,571
Megan Westwood, played by Sarah Jackson.

11
00:35:21,428 --> 00:35:27,428
Alice In Wonderland is a 2010 American Gothic dark fantasy adventure film directed by Tim Burton
from a screenplay written by Linda Woolverton and produced by Walt Disney Pictures.

12
00:38:34,285 --> 00:38:40,285
The film stars Mia Wasikowska in the live-action role, Johnny Depp, Anne Hathaway, Matt Lucas, Helena Bonham Carter, and Crispin Glover, and features the
voices of Alan Rickman, Stephen Fry, Michael Sheen, Timothy Spall, Christopher Lee, Paul Whitehouse, Barbara Windsor and Michael Gough.

13
00:41:47,142 --> 00:41:53,142
A live-action adaptation and remake of Lewis Carroll's works, the film follows Alice Kingsleigh, a nineteen-year-old who falls down a rabbit hole by going back to Wonderland, and
alongside the Mad Hatter helps restore the White Queen to her throne by fighting against the Red Queen and the Jabberwocky, a dragon who endangers Wonderland's residents.

14
00:45:00,000 --> 00:45:06,000
Alice in Wonderland began development in December 2007, when Burton was asked to
direct two 3D films for Disney, including the remake of Frankenweenie.

15
00:48:12,857 --> 00:48:18,857
Production began in September 2008 concluding within three months, and
was shot in the United Kingdom and the United States.

16
00:51:25,714 --> 00:51:31,714
It was followed by an extensive post-production and visual effects process
where filming included live-action and motion-capture sequences.

17
00:54:38,571 --> 00:54:44,571
Burton's frequent collaborator, Danny Elfman, composed an original theme for the film,
which premiered in London at the Odeon Leicester Square on February 25, 2010.

18
00:57:51,428 --> 00:57:57,428
It was released in the United Kingdom and the United States through the Disney Digital 3-D,
RealD 3D, and IMAX 3D formats as well as in standard theaters on March 5.

19
01:01:04,285 --> 01:01:10,285
The film generated over $1.025 billion in ticket sales and became the fifth highest-grossing film
during its theatrical run, and it is also the second-highest-grossing film of 2010.

20
01:04:17,142 --> 01:04:23,142
Amongst Disney's live-action adaptations, the film is tied for third-most-expensive,
alongside Mulan and the fourth-highest-grossing readaptation to date.

21
01:07:30,000 --> 01:07:36,000
It received three nominations at the 68th Golden Globe Awards
including for Best Motion Picture – Musical or Comedy.

22
01:10:42,857 --> 01:10:48,857
At the 83rd Academy Awards, it won Best Art Direction and Best
Costume Design, and was nominated for Best Visual Effects.

23
01:13:55,714 --> 01:14:01,714
The film received numerous other accolades.

24
01:17:08,571 --> 01:17:14,571
While not the first film in its genre, Alice in Wonderland is credited with starting a trend of
live-action fairy tale and fantasy films being green-lit, particularly from Walt Disney Studios.

25
01:20:21,428 --> 01:20:27,428
A follow-up film, titled Alice Through the Looking
Glass, was released on May 27, 2016.

26
01:23:34,285 --> 01:23:40,285
The film explores themes of small town, holiday,
high school sweetheart, christmas.

27
01:26:47,142 --> 01:26:53,142
The tone is emotional.
